---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Prose from "@/components/astro/Prose.astro";
import { DISCLAIMER } from "@/lib/site";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<PageLayout
  title="WhatsApp Chat Analyzer — Analyze Any WhatsApp Export Online, Privately"
  description="Analyze a WhatsApp chat export for message counts, activity patterns, emoji use and response times. A free browser-based WhatsApp chat analyzer with no upload and no sign-up."
  path="/whatsapp-chat-analyzer/"
>
  <Prose />
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold text-white">WhatsApp Chat Analyzer</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-zinc-300">
      A WhatsApp chat analyzer answers simple questions with real numbers: how many messages, who
      sends more, when the chat is most alive, which emoji carry the conversation. ChatWrapped is a
      free analyzer that runs the entire computation locally in your browser — the export file is
      never uploaded anywhere.
    </p>
    <a
      href={`${base}/app/`}
      class="mt-8 inline-block rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-600 to-fuchsia-600 px-7 py-3.5 text-base font-bold text-white shadow-xl shadow-fuchsia-950/40 transition hover:scale-[1.02]"
    >
      Analyze a chat now →
    </a>

    <div class="prose-cw">
      <h2>What ChatWrapped measures in a WhatsApp export</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Question</th><th>Metric</th><th>Where it appears</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr
            ><td>Who texts more?</td><td>Message share per participant</td><td
              >Overview · Story · Cards</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>When is the chat busiest?</td><td>Hour × weekday heatmap, monthly trend</td><td
              >Activity tab</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>How fast are replies?</td><td>Median / average response time (burst rule)</td><td
              >Responses tab · Story</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>Which emoji dominate?</td><td>Grapheme-safe emoji ranking</td><td
              >Emoji & words tab</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>What words define the chat?</td><td>Stopword-filtered word ranking</td><td
              >Emoji & words tab · Story</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>Who breaks the silence?</td><td>Conversation starts after a 4-hour lull</td><td
              >Records · Awards</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>Did we ever miss a day?</td><td>Longest consecutive active-day streak</td><td
              >Records · Story</td
            ></tr
          >
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Every metric’s exact definition, exclusions and edge cases are documented — nothing is a
        black box.
      </p>

      <h2>Analyzer features designed for privacy</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>No upload:</strong> the parser runs in a Web Worker on your device; no message text
          is ever transmitted.
        </li>
        <li><strong>No account:</strong> no sign-up, no email, no cookies for tracking.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Anonymization:</strong> replace participant names with “Participant A/B/…” before sharing
          screenshots.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Memory-only processing:</strong> parsed data lives in the tab; closing it clears everything.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Offline capable:</strong> after the first visit, the analyzer works without an internet
          connection.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>From analysis to shareable results</h2>
      <p>
        Numbers alone are dry, so ChatWrapped turns your analysis into a personalized story sequence
        and into high-resolution share cards in nine visual themes. Cards export as exact-size PNGs
        (story 1080×1920, portrait 1080×1350, square 1080×1080, landscape 1200×630) — individually
        or as a complete ZIP recap.
      </p>

      <h2>Why another WhatsApp analyzer?</h2>
      <p>
        Existing tools either upload your chat to a server, bury the privacy story, or stop at raw
        message counts. ChatWrapped is built around three principles: <strong
          >local processing</strong
        > (verifiable in your network tab),
        <strong>documented, reproducible metrics</strong> (every number has a written definition), and
        <strong>storytelling quality</strong> (themes, animation and card design you actually want to
        share).
      </p>

      <h3>Getting started</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <a href={`${base}/how-to-export-whatsapp-chat/`}>Export your WhatsApp chat</a> as TXT (without
          media).
        </li>
        <li>Open the <a href={`${base}/app/`}>analyzer</a> and drop the file in.</li>
        <li>Pick participants and a date range, then explore the dashboard, story and cards.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Prefer to look first? The analyzer has a clearly-labeled synthetic sample — no export
        required. Just press “Try a friends chat”.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-xs leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">{DISCLAIMER}</p>
  </main>
</PageLayout>
